      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A 256-bit key seals the vault. That key is held in the device Keychain behind Face ID, Touch ID, or your passcode, or behind an app password you set. The vault file on disk is useless without the key. An app password is mixed with a secret that never leaves this iPhone, so a copied vault can't be guessed at anywhere else, and the vault is kept out of iCloud and computer backups. Wrong guesses slow down after a few tries, and you can choose to erase the vault after 10." : {
      "comment" : "A description of how the vault is protected.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "a classic age identity, starting AGE-SECRET-KEY-1" : {
      "comment" : "A description of a Bech32 prefix for an age identity.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
