      "comment" : "A description of a Cocoa error that might occur when reading or writing a file.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A file with that name already exists." : {
      "comment" : "A file with that name already exists.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A hardware key's P-256 half is made inside the Secure Enclave and never leaves it. On iOS 26 and later both halves of a new quantum-safe hardware key live in the Secure Enclave, ML-KEM-768 included, and the vault keeps only handles that work on this iPhone alone. Existing quantum-safe hardware keys keep their ML-KEM half in the encrypted vault. On iOS 26 and later AgePony also uses Apple's CryptoKit for ML-KEM and the X25519 hybrid, after its own checks on every file and key; earlier iOS versions use AgePony's own code for them." : {
      "comment" : "A section of the security info view that describes how hardware keys are protected.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A hybrid key that keeps a file secret even if X25519 is broken by a future quantum computer. It cannot be combined with a classical recipient on the same file, because the weaker of the two would set the bar." : {
      "comment" : "A definition of a post-quantum key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A key made inside this iPhone's Secure Enclave, or one that lives on a YubiKey. The private half never leaves the hardware, so it can't be shown, sent or backed up. A Secure Enclave key is gone if the iPhone is erased or replaced, so encrypt important files to a second key as well (Also encrypt to, in Settings). A YubiKey decrypts with a tap over NFC, and its PIN when the key asks for it." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a hardware key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "A label for this signer, such as their name or email address. Shown when their signatures verify." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the name field for a signer.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
