    "AgePony bundles no third-party runtime libraries. The cryptography is built on Apple's CryptoKit, Security, and CommonCrypto, plus code written for this app where those frameworks stop short: SHA-3 and the SHAKE functions, ML-KEM-768, the HPKE hybrids, and the FIDO/CTAP2 stack for security keys. On iOS 26 and later CryptoKit's own ML-KEM-768 and X-Wing are used where age allows, and AgePony's code stays for earlier iOS and for the P-256 hybrid." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the dependencies of AgePony.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony can import SSH Ed25519 and RSA keys. This is another type." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when the user tries to import a key that is not Ed25519 or RSA.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony can't sign with %@ keys yet." : {
      "comment" : "A description of an error that might occur when signing files. The argument is the name of the key type.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony can't use %@ right now. Check that AgePony is allowed to use %@ in the Settings app." : {
      "comment" : "A message that says that Face ID only can't be used because the app doesn't have permission.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "AgePony can't use %1$@ right now. Check that AgePony is allowed to use %2$@ in the Settings app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "AgePony cannot protect a file once you decrypt it and hand it to another app. It cannot recover a lost password. It cannot stop someone who already holds your unlocked phone, which is what the duress password is for. On iOS it cannot fully block screenshots: it hides content in the app switcher and blurs private keys, but a screenshot on an unlocked screen is still possible." : {
      "comment" : "A description of what AgePony cannot do.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony doesn't use %@ keys here." : {
      "comment" : "A description of an error that might occur when decrypting a file with an SSH key. The argument is the type of key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony doesn't use %@ keys." : {
      "comment" : "A description of an error that might occur when opening an SSH key. The argument is the type of key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony encrypts and decrypts files and text on your device using the age format, and signs and verifies them with SSH keys. Nothing is uploaded. There is no account and no server." : {
      "comment" : "A description of how AgePony works.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony encrypts files, text and notes with age, and your keys stay on this iPhone." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the app's features.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony is an independent app built on the open age format and is not affiliated with the age project." : {
