      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "AgePony uses the network for two things, and only when you ask: fetching a recipient's public keys from GitHub, which can go through an HTTP proxy you set, and sending keys straight to your other phone on the same Wi-Fi. The second stays on your local network and carries only data encrypted to the receiving phone's one-time key. Everything else runs offline." : {
