    },
    "Encryption only, and safe against a future quantum computer. Files stay secret even if X25519 is broken later. Readable by the age CLI 1.3 and newer. A post-quantum recipient can't be combined with a classical one on the same file, since the weaker of the two would set the bar." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a post-quantum age key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encryption only, quantum-safe" : {
      "comment" : "A description of a Secure Enclave-backed identity",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encryption only, quantum-safe. On iOS 26 and later both halves of a new quantum-safe hardware key, P-256 and ML-KEM-768, live in the Secure Enclave. A file needs both to open. Keys made before keep their ML-KEM half in the encrypted vault. Readable by age 1.3 or newer." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a post-quantum key that lives in the Secure Enclave.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encryption only, quantum-safe. The P-256 half lives in the Secure Enclave and the ML-KEM-768 half is kept in the encrypted vault. A file needs both to open. On iOS 26 and later both halves of a new key live in the Secure Enclave. Readable by age 1.3 or newer." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a secure-enclave-backed P-256 key.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encryption only, quantum-safe. The Secure Enclave couldn't make the ML-KEM-768 half of this key, so the P-256 half lives in the Secure Enclave and the ML-KEM-768 half is kept in the encrypted vault. A file needs both to open. Readable by age 1.3 or newer." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a post-quantum key that's backed by the Secure Enclave.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Encryption only. The private key is made inside this iPhone's Secure Enclave and decryption happens there, so it never leaves the hardware. Anyone can encrypt to it with age 1.3 or newer, or AgePony on Android." : {
