    },
    "When on, AgePony automatically adds your active identity as a recipient on every file you encrypt, so you can still decrypt it yourself later. \"Also encrypt to\" ticks a saved recipient by default too: pick a key you have backed up, so a file you encrypt to this iPhone's hardware key can still be opened if the phone is lost." : {
      "comment" : "Footnote for the encryption settings.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "When on, AgePony prompts for %@ before revealing private keys or decrypting sensitive notes. How the vault itself locks is set under Lock & password." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the security settings in the settings view. The argument is the string “Face ID”, the string “Touch ID”, the string “Optic ID”, or the value of the localized string key “your passcode”.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "When on, entering the app %@ wrong %lld times in a row erases the vault, the same way the duress %@ does but without opening an empty vault afterwards. Keep a backup of your keys if you turn this on." : {
      "comment" : "A paragraph describing the effect of toggling \"Erase after 5 wrong tries\" on the vault.",
